 me and this  is compounded by some of them being much  older than what they're actually playing  for example rhaenys and viserys are  supposed to be in their mid to early 20s  at the Council of 101 and when I checked  by asking my wife how old she thought  they were supposed to be she guessed  much closer to the actors ages in real  life it's a small thing and we are going  to be moving forward in time anyway but  it really kind of got on my nerves when  I went back to take my notes they pulled  off the attorney and the jousting  especially that shot of Damon sliding  over the rail and some pretty badass  armor and I like that they aren't shying  away from keeping it as a show for  grown-ups by including the nudity and  sex which are a big part of how these  folks spend their down time in the books  they managed to make most of the  characters seem interesting even though  they didn't spend much time with any any  of them for example Auto seems like a  scheming douche especially after he sent  his young daughter to the king's  Chambers to comfort him while wearing  one of her mother's dresses but he's a  necessary douche and you get that Beyond  being absolutely caught up in his  distaste for Damon he's effective at his  job after all while viserys is likable  enough it seems apparent that ruling the  realm is in his strong suit and don't  take my word for it or Patty  constadine's great depiction of that the  fact that he keeps getting cut by the  Iron Throne is really the only evidence  you need I guess the next trick they  have to pull off is to flesh out the  main characters and make us want to  watch them if we can't root for them  sometimes there's a welcome honesty  present in watching bad people do bad  things as it speaks to the  irredeemability of the systems that  perpetuate the underlying conditions and  sometimes it's just viscerally  satisfying to watch fictional depictions  of people tearing each other apart the  show will no doubt deliver those things  in equal amounts what I hope is that  I'll be tuning in because I care what  happens rather than just not being able  to look away I think the dragons will  keep some people coming back but the  question of why they're not around  during a game of thrones is gonna start  to hang over things I mean a part of  even the most casual fan must know that  it's not like they formed a union and  decided to live out their lives in the  Hills after retirement so I'll be  interested to see how people experience  that and I think that's a good place to  leave things let me know in the comments  what you thought about the premiere and  what you're hoping to see in the  upcoming episodes I'm not sure if I'm  gonna do episode Recaps throughout the  whole season this is going to be a  saturated space so if no one watches  them I'm not sure I'll be putting this  much time in each week but I'll  definitely be watching the show and will  probably make different videos instead  so please like this video If you enjoyed  it please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already and thanks for for  watching I'll talk to you soon

